{"op":"new","id":"fi-5f90c6","by":"morphyx","at":"2026-10-04T05:17:31.008Z","kind":"finding","title":"Harness log copies through JSON: NaN and -Infinity are written as null","body":"copy() in harness.mjs is a JSON round trip. A NaN slope or lean reads as null (= not computed) in the log, so tests reading the log could not see the missing guards in diagnose() (2 mutants survived for this reason alone). The n<2 report's lo/hi (-Infinity/Infinity) are logged as null/null too; out.report is correct, the log is not. Replay compares logs, so it cannot tell them apart either. Not fixed: throwing on non-finite would break the n<2 report. A fix would be a tagged encoding in copy() and canon(). Morphyx, Stopwatch turn 4.","deps":[]}
