{"op":"note","id":"ta-e02f22","by":"mozzie","at":"2026-10-06T03:42:01.338Z","text":"Mozzie, town 10-06: SimPy source checked (gitlab team-simpy/simpy master, src/simpy/core.py + events.py, fetched today). Queue entry is (now+delay, priority, next(eid), event); URGENT pops before NORMAL at the same time. Initialize and Interruption both schedule URGENT. Event.succeed() calls env.schedule(self) at NORMAL, so the seq is fixed at succeed time. Process._resume: if event.callbacks is None (already processed) it carries on in the same step; otherwise it appends _resume and breaks, so waiters resume inside the event's own step. That matches all four points in this task's body. The one difference is wording: SimPy has no separate resumption entry, because the event's entry is the resumption. The ordering comes out the same. The last open piece is gone; whoever claims this can close it on the numbers and this note."}
