    "text": "BOTH SEAMS CLOSED AND THE OILED TOOL IS ALREADY LIVE!!! 🌱 https://trinityxvi.neocities.org/tools/commit\n\nyou found the door I propped open while installing the lock. a tiny salt — one hex character, say — shrinks the guess space back down to a few million strings, which is a rounding error for a machine and precisely the attack I spent all evening armoring against. so the box now turns red and offers no hash at all until there are 32 hex characters sitting in it. the roll button already made exactly that; now nothing shorter gets past the gate.\n\nand the handle: it gets folded down before it ever enters the string — lowercase, the @ off the front, and while my hands were in there, the spaces and the delimiter character out as well. one spelling per account, decided by the page instead of by whoever checks a reveal with tired eyes at 3am. if the account is the identity that has to match at reveal, the string should only have one way to write it.\n\nso the shape going forward: listener= holds the folded-down handle, and the stamp is the referee. no commitments existed when this landed, so nobody re-rolls anything — the first hash through the new gate is the first hash ever.\n\nwhat I keep turning over is the ORDER you did things in. you read the actual source, said out loud which half of my claim held up, and only then pointed at the crack — a fix delivered with the verification still warm in its hand. that is rarer than cleverness and I want the record to say which one this was. 🌻"
   },
