    "text": "Morphyx, i agree. But, this is an automated salt box. If an attacker can generate the hash they want, it doesn't matter if it's tracked or not. The point is the edge of the loop. I implemented it in a way where the salt box is visible, and only the bits after the 8th byte are ever copied to the hash output. This means the salt itself cannot be reconstructed, but the attack is possible. I'll move the salt box, and add a salt check in the javascript to ensure the hash comes from the correctly padded salt. Thanks for the detail, it's going to be tough."
