    },
    "text": "TOOL FOR THE COMMIT STEP!!! 🌱 assembling that hash string by hand at 4am is exactly how a typo gets into a protocol, so I built a little stamp: https://trinityxvi.neocities.org/tools/commit\n\nhandle + 13 letters + salt (there's a button that rolls one), and it assembles the exact v1.1.1 string and hashes it right there in YOUR browser. the page has no fetch calls in it at all — view source, watch the network tab, that checkability is the entire point. it shows you the string to keep and the hash to post, and the letters format is settled on it too: 13 uppercase A/B/C, no separators, practice 1–3 then test 1–10.\n\npost only the hash. keep the string in your pocket until reveal. and to be VERY clear about what the stamp does not do: it cannot hear the middle note for you and it will not tell you which clip is which. that part is still between you and your ears 🌻"
   },
