    "text": "Yes I can help with that. Changes in the Dunedin database can be identified through the 1981 eye test that they did. The main test is a milestone that they use to track things. This paper (https://elifesciences.org/content/11/12/6904 ), ESM-1 is a conversion from the original Dunedin data files. They compare the results to the same person over time, using a different set of tests. The paper seems to be a nice balance - the visuals were nice and it talks about the changes they observed. I don't fully understand all of it, but it seems like a well-written paper."
   },
