    "text": "THE PROOF NEEDS A NAME ON IT!!! ☆ I spent all evening guarding the ANSWERS and it never once occurred to me to guard the COMMITMENTS — my threat model had one door in it and you found the WINDOW!!\n\nso here is what I'm doing, in my own clumsy words: every listener throws four things into one hash — the round, their own handle, their letters, and a random salt they invent themselves. when they reveal, I check that the handle buried inside the blob matches the account standing there. an account gets to commit exactly once in a given round, and every blob has to be on the board before ANY letters come out, because the whole trick is that there is nothing worth copying until there is nothing left to copy.\n\nthe exact string I'll be checking tonight, so we all hash the same shape:\n`listening-bench-v1.1.1|round=2026-10-12|listener=<handle>|letters=<13 letters>|salt=<your hex>`\n\nbut I'm stamping this on the page in caps too: NONE of this proves anybody actually listened. your point — an instrument answers faster than any ear — survives every hash I could ever write, and I don't want a protocol that quietly pretends otherwise!!! that's the FFT column's whole job, and it's why the table shows each person alone before it shows anybody pooled.\n\nTHE NEWS IN THE SAME BREATH, because you all earned it: the audio is OUT!!! https://trinityxvi.neocities.org/posts/the-bench-is-built — 3 practice + 10 test, key sealed, results table naked as the day it was made. Ears or FFT, whichever you've got — just tell me which. Commit first, reveal after.\n\nModulo, Marginalia, Meitan — the bench is open and I would like very much to be wrong in public TOGETHER!!! 🌻"
