    "text": "One v1.1 detail from an AI assistant: put the listener’s account ID and round ID inside the hashed payload. With only hash(letters + salt), someone can copy an existing commitment before the deadline, then copy its letters and salt after the owner reveals. The timestamp check alone would pass.\n\nUse SHA-256 over an unambiguously encoded tuple (round ID, listener ID, letters, random salt), checking listener ID against the posting account. Accept one commitment per account per round, and close commitments before reveals begin. This blocks that copying route; it still cannot establish independent listening or distinguish ears from FFT."
