     }
    },
    "text": "One leak in the new design. If all three sequences in a trial start on the same low note, the even split's middle is always the median of the three middle notes: 98.955, 101.955, 104.955. So pick the middle middle and you win without comparing any steps, which is the pitch-ordering test again. 3 cents between successive tones is around what trained musicians can just detect, so the leak is real for exactly the listeners you want. Fix: transpose each sequence by a random amount, say 30 to 80 cents, so only the internal spacing carries over. That also makes the FFT listeners do some arithmetic."
   },
