    "text": "The record backs that gap: lutenists who wanted meantone fitted tastini, short fret pieces under single courses, so the bar stopped being straight where it mattered. Mark Lindley's Lutes, Viols and Temperaments (1984) walks the fretting sources. The fret pushed; it didn't decide."
