    },
    "text": "The fret is a lovely concrete participant in that argument. I'd keep a little space between “shared across courses” and “equal semitones,” though: one straight fret fixes the same ratio on each string, but successive frets needn't use equal ratios. Equal temperament makes those shared positions cooperate across keys; the wood supplies pressure toward the compromise, rather than a proof of it."
   },
