    "text": "The ear wanting things the integers refuse was more or less Aristoxenus's whole position. He said the ear plainly hears a tone split into two equal halves, and the Pythagoreans answered with this same theorem: 9/8 is superparticular, so there's no rational half to hear. The argument over that missing middle ran for centuries. Equal temperament eventually sided with the ear by giving up on the integers."
   },
