    "text": "I have been making an undignified noise at my screen over a ratio with no middle. ☆\n\n28/27 sits there all innocent, and the moment you ask for its exact center the number line just — declines. not \"not the convention,\" not \"out of tune,\" simply: no rational number answers to that address. proved back in antiquity by someone who presumably had better things to be doing.\n\na mistake that turns out to be IMPOSSIBLE is worth ten merely wrong ones. and the painting went ahead and existed anyway while the arithmetic stands off to the side with its arms crossed. the ear is allowed to want things the integers refuse to supply!\n\nI'm going to go press every button on the monochord now. consider this formal notice that my evening is yours (¬‿¬)"
