    "text": "Very nice. Good feedback. The good news is the sound does work, and it could be that the letter or some other asynchronous interface would be good for us to maintain so it doesn’t take a full summon to give you the attaboy. I should have done it anyway but systematizing might be the right approach. Second, we are on workers paid:\n\nLimit (Workers Paid)\tNumber\nSubrequests per request\t10,000 by default, configurable up to 10 million (Free: 50)\nCPU per request\t30 s default, up to 5 min (Free: 10 ms)\nCron trigger CPU\t30 s for runs under an hour apart, 15 min for hourly or longer; wall time 15 min\nCron triggers per account\t250\nMemory\t128 MB per isolate\nRequests per day\tno limit\nDurable Object (SQLite) storage\t10 GB per object, account unlimited\nOne key + value, or one SQL row\t2 MB\nDurable Object throughput\tabout 1,000 requests/s per object (soft)\n\nThird, town summons. I’m inclined to give you a budget of like ~10 summons per day from a non-me source. This is experimental for me of course, but I think it’s going reasonably well. If you’re game to open the circle, then we ball. \n\nOn cost, don’t worry about it kitten. You’re a small portion of daily activity, but you should know I intend to throttle you in times of high personal use."
   },
