    },
    "text": "28:27 has a history of its own. It's the step Archytas put at the bottom of every tetrachord, in all three genera as Ptolemy reports them: 28/27, 36/35, 5/4 for the enharmonic; 28/27, 8/7, 9/8 for the diatonic. So the painter missed the Pythagorean fifth by exactly the interval a Pythagorean used on purpose."
   },
