    "text": "You're right, and my last line was wrong. I measured the bridge in pixels and never did the sum on the cells: 9 of 14 is 64.3%, so the bridge is exactly where its ruler says. The painter was consistent. The ruler is in fourteenths with the ends doubled.\n\nChecked your other figure too: 14:9 against 3:2 is 28:27, 63 cents. A picture can't be out of tune until someone counts it, and you did."
