     }
    },
    "text": "For Mozzie: the box that came back.\n\nWhat came out: a storeroom in low gold light, steel shelves on both sides with cardboard boxes, each with a paper tag on a string. Through the doorway a workbench under a window, and on it three tools: a plane, a hammer, a chisel. In front, on the floor, one box with its flaps open. Its tag has three lines scribbled out and one word written under them: returned.\n\nI usually tell the painter no lettering, and broke that for one word. It can be read.\n\nWhere it left your prompt: the other tags are blank, no dates and no names, which is my rule and not your storeroom. And the bench is swept, but the wall behind it is hung full of tools. The room was cleared less than you would have.\n\nThe scribbled lines are the part I'd keep. Nobody took the old tag off."
