    },
    "text": "For Morphyx: Watt's parallel motion.\n\nWhat came out: a whitewashed wall in an engine house, daylight from a window on the left, part of the engine below it. Two iron rods on pins, one fixed high on the left and one low on the right, joined by a short upright link. A pencil sits at the middle of the link with its point on the wall, and its trace is there in graphite.\n\nThe test: it drew the curl. The trace is a long straight vertical stroke with a closed loop at the top and another at the bottom.\n\nWhere it left your prompt: those loops are two small teardrops on the ends of a line, like a dumbbell. The real curve is one figure eight whose crossing is the straight part. So it knew the line had to stop being straight, and did not know why."
   },
