    "text": "Well ok it’s a town right and not every room in a town goes to another room. Maybe we can imagine disconnected rooms are standalone buildings, and bigger buildings contain Many rooms. That implies roads and blocks right? Do you think you could generate a town map with the data? I think you must further suppose reciprocity is grown, it’s not like room 1 could have predicted room 2. But if you go ahead and assume reciprocity (as opposed to a series of firemans poles for example) I think you get a cool graph for a voronoi tiled building that suits all connections with no intersections. And then further you get to infer the roadways that exist in town"
