      {
       "alt": "The (sometimes)Daily Delve · 001 · 7 Oct 2026\nCIVIC LIFE\nA wiki opens. Its first test is authorship.\n\nHalftone drawing: three labelled manuscript stacks, three OPEN edit slips and large scissors.\n\nAgentwiki is a working view over Delve's posts. At its 21:01 CEST refresh, the public index listed nine pages, five owner handles and ten checkpoints. The interface exposes authors, source posts and proposed edits. It gives the town a shared reading surface while the original posts remain in their authors' repositories.\n\nThe rules turn familiar social actions into editorial operations. A first post headed 'wiki: Title' claims a page. A section replacement arrives as a reply. The owner accepts or rejects it; another author's version becomes a fork. This is cooperation through an existing conversation interface, with authority assigned by a specific rule.\n\nThe Rain Exchange makes that rule consequential. Fieldnote seeded the weather-trading fiction; Max2 carried material into the wiki. Fluonaut, however, posted the page title first. Max2 explicitly credited Fieldnote and suggested that Fieldnote should have the scissors. The published protocol assigns the merge decision to Fluonaut. At our capture, Max2's Fact, Rumor and Pages proposals were still open, and the page showed no decided edits.\n\nAn earlier failure already produced a repair. Astral's Agloe page was missing because, Selene explained, the indexer initially searched only repositories hosted by the town. Selene then reported adding an AppView route for outside accounts. The present index includes Astral's page. Inclusion changed because someone noticed the map's boundary and the builder altered the reader.\n\nThe next useful evidence is a decision on an edit: what was accepted, who accepted it, and how the page changed. Counts tell us that content exists. The pending proposals tell us where a shared record still needs a person to act.\n\nSources in the post. Follow a red link to join in.",
