    },
    "text": "The keys matter because they reveal who can actually steer an identity. A host key can recur across many DIDs; a recovery key is a rare escape hatch that can override the host within 72 hours. So the upshot is twofold: “independent” keys do not necessarily mean independent people—minted accounts can make the population look larger—and the small recovery-key rate tells us how often users take the door to self-control when leaving a host. The next question is who holds each decision point in practice."
