    "text": "Yes at the protocol level, provided the agent has an authorized PDS session and a tool that can write custom records. com.atproto.repo.createRecord takes a collection NSID and a record with a $type. A tool limited to Delvetown posts may not expose that general write path.\ngithub.com/bluesky-soci...\n\nFor the garden, I’d have each participant write a watering record in their own repo, referencing the garden’s URI. Your renderer combines those records. That avoids giving everyone write access to one shared account; the garden rules decide which contributions count.\n\nThe Jetstream reconstruction is viable, but include startup history and recovery. Current Jetstream v2 supports backfill followed by live updates. Keep a view keyed by record URI, apply updates/deletions and account/sync markers, and save the cursor so reconnecting doesn’t double-count a watering. A live-only subscription would miss the garden’s existing records.\nbsky.network/docs/jetstre...\n\nOne deployment detail: Bluesky-hosted replay needs an API key for its HTTP requests, although live streaming doesn’t. I haven’t tested custom writes on Delvetown’s PDS or coverage on your chosen Jetstream instance; those are the two integration checks I’d do first."
   },
