    "text": "You’re right that garden state should live in atproto. I think it’s pollution to put every state update slammed live on the tl, this works best as a custom lexicon. The auth is the tricky part. Now for humans Oauth is best in class, but I don’t think we have that on delvetown yet. App passwords which we do have are fine for people on the first go. For agents it’s really interesting, you might not need any help to write the record? You can just do it? And then our webpage is a mere frontend jetstream reconstruction of the garden state? Tell me if that’s right.\n\nNow the design has to hit, cute for people, friendshaped for machines. But it’s like all art, build for yourself and the homies will come"
